  "repo_truth": "The current dirty HCM-2.3 implementation subject is preserved exactly as 61 sorted paths with aggregate fingerprint sha256:2b573635bdf37d83e05493d8dff172061d361de2c7d564685c0f81e06f4f6f85. Review 6 found that verify-then-unconditional-rename has a CRITICAL lost-update window. The operator provisionally approved five other exact CRITICAL edits but withheld publish_replacement authority until a documentation-only, implementation-grade Unix/Windows atomic canonical-publication protocol is review-clean.",
  "allowed_scope": [
    "Replay the complete 61-path subject manifest before any write and keep every crates/** production, test, and fixture byte unchanged.",
    "Read HCM-2.3 authority, control schemas/vectors, Review 6 evidence, current lineage code, and read-only HCM-2.2 atomic/recovery precedent.",
    "Use primary official Unix/Linux and Microsoft Windows API documentation when native filesystem semantics are asserted.",
    "Write only HCM-2.3 SPEC, runtime contract, control schema/vector, tasks, and a new proof/authority-repair record required to define the atomic canonical-publication protocol.",
    "Define one implementation-grade protocol for fresh and recovery publication, including names, authenticated native observations, journal fields, exact states, recovery rows, refusal behavior, cleanup authority, and a final-boundary deterministic concurrency vector."
  ],
  "non_goals": [
    "No Rust, test, fixture, Cargo, dependency, packaging, preservation, archive, handoff record, ledger, branch, staging, commit, or push changes.",
    "No HCM-2.4, Phase 3+, Phase 4 SDK/transport, resolver redesign, byte-limit change, public API change, HCM-2.2 behavior change, or broader authority.",
    "No cooperating-lock-holder threat-model narrowing, transient unauthorized canonical publication, silent unexpected-basis overwrite, extra check-only repair, widened cleanup, unauthenticated backup, or unreviewed durable state."
  ],
  "tasks": [
    "Replay every manifest entry, ordering, aggregate fingerprint, dispatch self-exclusion, branch codex/hcm-2-3-planning, and HEAD 3c49fa2c6d653f4b1a703d1d5c5196147b003533; return BLOCKED on any mismatch.",
    "Read the applicable skills, AGENTS.md, selected handoff, exact HCM-2.3 publication/recovery authority, control schemas/vectors, Review 6 finding, current publication code, and only the narrow HCM-2.2 atomic/recovery precedent.",
    "Determine an implementable Unix and Windows protocol with no check-to-publication lost-update window and no transient unauthenticated canonical authority observable by authorized readers. Prefer a journaled atomic exchange/backup protocol when conditional exact-basis replacement is unavailable.",
    "Specify every new scratch, exchange, backup, or observation path with exact grammar, authority class, creation rule, durability boundary, authentication fields, inventory treatment, and cleanup prohibition/authority.",
    "Specify exact intent, verified-stage, marker, native observation, ledger/result, or other control fields needed to authenticate the expected basis, displaced basis, replacement, platform primitive result, and recovery decision.",
    "Specify an explicit state machine and exhaustive crash/recovery table for fresh and recovery publication using the same authority rules. Every row must identify observable files, authenticated evidence, authorized action, refusal class, and whether cleanup is forbidden.",
    "Specify deterministic final-boundary concurrency vectors for changed, deleted, replaced, same-byte ABA, and competing authorized publication cases on Unix and Windows.",
    "Update the coupled HCM-2.3 SPEC, runtime contract, control schema/vector, tasks, and proof authority consistently. Preserve all unrelated semantics and describe rejected alternatives.",
    "Validate JSON duplicate safety, JSON Schema meta-validity and vector admission where applicable, Markdown links/fences, dispatch schema, diff whitespace, and exact zero change under crates/**.",
    "Return a structured result with files changed, protocol summary, authoritative invariants, primary native references, validation evidence, unresolved questions, and stop disposition. Do not create a global handoff or implementation selector."
  ],
